// Once-per-select consumption with a SHARED input
// (design/wake_catchup.md): both arms read in1, so its fires are
// always consumed by whichever arm is awake — the woken arm gets ZERO
// catch-up fires and its value correctness comes entirely from the
// forced recompute (the publish-shaped probe that proved tracking
// alone insufficient). Flip to false after in1 -> 9: recompute reads
// the present 9, emits 27 stale-value/fired-select.
// Expected trace (both engines): 0; 10; 18; 27.
// schedule-v1: cap=208 events=1664; in0=bool:true in1=i64:5; in1=i64:9; in0=bool:false
{let v0 = select in0 {true => in1 * i64:2, false => in1 * i64:3}; v0}
